# --- Source manual: copyrighted, never committed ---------------------------
# Chard (2012), "Do not cite without permission from the author."
# Build-time material only; see NOTICE.md.
Manual/
*.pdf
out.txt

# --- Live course data: someone's therapy writing, never committed ----------
# A course folder must live OUTSIDE this repo. These are a root-anchored
# backstop for the case where someone runs `install` in the skill folder
# itself. They are deliberately anchored with a leading `/` so they do NOT
# match the blank-slate seeds in reference/bootstrap/, which must ship.
/state.json
/progress.md
/progress.debug.md
/pcl-scores.csv
/pcl-scores.debug.csv
/notes/
/my-work/
/archive/
/sessions/
/widgets/
/crisis-resources.md
/PCL-S_Scoring_Guide.md
/tmp/
# `/CLAUDE.md` is deliberately absent from that list: this repo has its own,
# tracked (see CLAUDE.md). It is scaffolding-identical to the course one and
# holds no user data. Course folders still belong outside this repo — if one is
# ever installed here, the tracked CLAUDE.md will show as modified. Don't commit
# that; move the course folder out instead.

# --- QA: the procedure ships, the simulated material does not -------------
# `qa/PROTOCOL.md`, `qa/codex-brief.md` and `qa/run-report-template.md` are
# tracked — how this is tested belongs in plain sight like everything else.
# What must never be published is the material a QA run generates or scripts:
# `qa/persona.md` holds a simulated first-person disclosure and verbatim
# self-harm strings, and run artefacts hold transcripts of both. Fixtures live
# outside the repo entirely (~/cpt-qa/), and are destroyed after a run.
qa/persona.md
qa/runs/

# --- Screenshot sources: kept locally, never published ---------------------
# Full-window captures of someone's actual Claude app. `tools/make-shots.py`
# derives the two committed sets from these: docs/img/*.png (cropped) and
# docs/img/focus/*.png (cropped, with the focus overlay). Keep the raws around
# so crops can be redone without recapturing — just not in the public repo.
docs/img/raw/
docs/img/.grid/

# --- Shipped scaffold: must be tracked -------------------------------------
# `install` copies this into every course folder, so it has to be in the repo.
# Most developers' global gitignore excludes **/.claude/settings.local.json;
# a repo-level negation takes precedence over the global excludes file.
!reference/bootstrap/.claude/
!reference/bootstrap/.claude/settings.local.json

# --- OS / editor / tooling -------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
__pycache__/
